      <p>
        Notice what the plot does and does not show. The estimates themselves are remarkably stable
        — somewhere between an 8% and a 12% reduction, every time. Nobody has found calcium to be
        harmful to bone. The argument is about whether a reduction that small, in people who were
        not short of calcium to begin with, is worth prescribing to everyone.
      </p>

